"\n<div class=\"brand-bar\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"brand-logo\"><div class=\"brand-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div></div>\n<header class=\"lk-hd\"><div class=\"lk-topic\"><svg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M3.5 9.2A8.3 8.3 0 1 1 3.2 13\"></path><path d=\"M3.2 4.2v5h5\"></path><path d=\"M12 8.3V12l3 1.8\"></path></svg></div><div class=\"lk-kicker\">Lektion</div><div class=\"lk-big\">13</div><h1>과거형</h1><div class=\"lk-de\">Das Präteritum</div><div class=\"lk-intro\">과거형은 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요 — ich lernte · ich ging · ich war.<br>글·이야기·뉴스에서 주로 쓰고, 말할 때는 sein·haben·화법조동사와 몇몇 동사를 과거형으로 써요.<br>이 과에서는 규칙 동사의 -te, 불규칙 동사의 모음 변화, 혼합 동사, 그리고 sein·haben·화법조동사의 과거형을 정리해요.<div class=\"x-goals\"><div class=\"x-goals-t\">이 과에서 익힐 것</div><div class=\"x-goal\">현재완료와 과거형을 쓰는 상황을 구별해요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">규칙 동사는 어간 + te + 어미로 만들어요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">불규칙 동사의 과거 어간을 외우고 어미를 붙여요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">혼합 동사 dachte·brachte·kannte·wusste를 써요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">sein·haben·werden과 화법조동사의 과거형을 써요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">동사의 세 형태(원형·과거형·과거분사)를 한 세트로 외워요</div></div></div></header>\n<div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge review-badge\">복습</span><span class=\"sub-title\">10–12과 복습</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Ich ____ gestern nach Hause gegangen.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) bin</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) habe</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) hat</button></div><div class=\"qe\">장소 이동 → sein (12과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> besuchen의 과거분사는?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) besucht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) begesucht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) gebesucht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) besuchen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">비분리 → ge 없음 (12과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Er ____ das Auto in die Garage gefahren.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) sind</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) haben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) hat</button></div><div class=\"qe\">4격 목적어가 있으면 haben (12과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> '나는 7시에 일어나야 해요.'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Ich muss um 7 Uhr stehen auf.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ich muss um 7 Uhr aufstehe.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Ich muss um 7 Uhr aufstehen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Ich muss aufstehen um 7 Uhr.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">화법조동사 + 원형 끝 (10·11과).</div></div></div>\n<section id=\"sec-A\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">A</span><h2>한국어로 먼저 보기</h2></div><p>한국어 과거는 말할 때나 글을 쓸 때나 같아요 — '나는 어제 영화를 봤다'.<br>독일어는 과거 시제가 두 가지이고, 말과 글에서 나눠 써요.<br>말할 때는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재완료<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재완료</span>말할 때 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. haben/sein + 과거분사로 만들어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.</span></span></span>(12과), 글과 이야기에서는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>이에요.</p><div class=\"dgm\"><div class=\"dgm-cap\">같은 과거, 말과 글에서 다른 시제</div><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>상황</th><th>독일어</th><th>시제</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>친구에게 말할 때</td><td>Ich <strong>habe</strong> gestern einen Film <strong>gesehen</strong>.</td><td>현재완료</td></tr><tr><td>일기·소설·기사</td><td>Gestern <strong>sah</strong> ich einen Film.</td><td>과거형</td></tr><tr><td>말할 때 · sein</td><td>Ich <strong>war</strong> gestern im Kino.</td><td>과거형</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"dgm-note\">뜻은 같아요. 차이는 말투와 글투예요. sein·haben·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">화법조동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">화법조동사</span>능력·허락·의무·의지 같은 뜻을 더해 주는 동사예요. 본동사는 원형으로 문장 끝에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: können · dürfen · müssen · sollen · wollen · mögen</span></span></span>는 말할 때도 과거형이 더 자연스러워요.</div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-B\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">B</span><h2>언제 과거형을 쓰나요</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">말할 때는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재완료<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재완료</span>말할 때 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. haben/sein + 과거분사로 만들어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.</span></span></span>, 글과 이야기에서는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>을 주로 써요. 다만 sein·haben·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">화법조동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">화법조동사</span>능력·허락·의무·의지 같은 뜻을 더해 주는 동사예요. 본동사는 원형으로 문장 끝에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: können · dürfen · müssen · sollen · wollen · mögen</span></span></span>는 말할 때도 과거형을 써요 — Ich <strong>war</strong> krank.</p></div></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" alt=\"Ich habe Deutsch gelernt. 말할 때 — 현재완료 / Ich lernte Deutsch. 글에서 — 과거형\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption class=\"ph-pair\"><div><span class=\"ph-de\">Ich <strong>habe</strong> Deutsch <strong>gelernt</strong>.</span><span class=\"ph-ko\">말할 때 — 현재완료</span></div><div><span class=\"ph-de\">Ich <strong>lernte</strong> Deutsch.</span><span class=\"ph-ko\">글과 이야기에서 — 과거형</span></div></figcaption></figure><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>상황</th><th>주로 쓰는 시제</th><th>예</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>대화 · 메시지 · 편지</td><td>현재완료</td><td>Ich <strong>habe</strong> viel <strong>gearbeitet</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>글 · 이야기 · 뉴스 · 보고서</td><td>과거형</td><td>Der Zug <strong>kam</strong> zu spät an.</td></tr><tr><td>sein · haben · 화법조동사 (말할 때도)</td><td>과거형</td><td>Ich <strong>war</strong> müde. · Ich <strong>hatte</strong> Hunger. · Ich <strong>musste</strong> arbeiten.</td></tr><tr><td>es gab · wusste · dachte (말할 때도 자주)</td><td>과거형</td><td>Es <strong>gab</strong> keine Tickets mehr. · Das <strong>wusste</strong> ich nicht.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-C\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">C</span><h2>규칙 동사 — 어간 + te + 어미</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">규칙 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어간<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어간</span>동사원형에서 끝의 -en(-n)을 뗀 부분이에요. 여기에 인칭어미를 붙여요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen → lern-</span></span></span> 뒤에 -te를 붙이면 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>이 돼요 — lernen → ich lern<strong>te</strong> · wir lern<strong>ten</strong>.</p></div></div><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-first\"><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>어미</th><th>lernen</th><th>arbeiten</th><th>studieren</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ich</td><td>-te</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">te</span></td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">ete</span></td><td>studier<span class=\"x-e\">te</span></td></tr><tr><td>du</td><td>-test</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">test</span></td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">etest</span></td><td>studier<span class=\"x-e\">test</span></td></tr><tr><td>er · sie · es</td><td>-te</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">te</span></td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">ete</span></td><td>studier<span class=\"x-e\">te</span></td></tr><tr><td>wir</td><td>-ten</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">ten</span></td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">eten</span></td><td>studier<span class=\"x-e\">ten</span></td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td>-tet</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">tet</span></td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">etet</span></td><td>studier<span class=\"x-e\">tet</span></td></tr><tr><td>sie · Sie</td><td>-ten</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">ten</span></td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">eten</span></td><td>studier<span class=\"x-e\">ten</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-key\"><span class=\"co-badge \">ich = er, 그리고 -t·-d 어간의 -e-</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">과거형은 ich와 er의 모양이 같아요 — ich lernte · er lernte.<br>어간이 -t·-d로 끝나면 -e-를 넣어요 — arbeitete · wartete · redete (5과 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재형</span>지금의 일, 습관, 가까운 미래를 말할 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich lerne Deutsch.</span></span></span>과 같은 원리).</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">규칙 동사 과거형</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Gestern ____ ich lange. <span class=\"qh\">arbeiten</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) arbeitet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) arbeitte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) arbeitete</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) arbeitetet</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -t → arbeit + ete.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Wir ____ in Seoul. <span class=\"qh\">wohnen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) wohnten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) wohnen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) wohnte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) wohntet</button></div><div class=\"qe\">wir → -ten.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Er ____ Medizin. <span class=\"qh\">studieren</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) studierten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) studiertete</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) studiert</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) studierte</button></div><div class=\"qe\">er → -te (ich와 같아요).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> ____ du gestern Fußball? <span class=\"qh\">spielen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Spieltet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Spieltest</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Spielte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Spielst</button></div><div class=\"qe\">du → -test.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-D\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">D</span><h2>불규칙 동사 — 과거 어간 + 어미</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">불규칙 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 모음이 바뀐 과거 모양을 따로 외워요 — gehen → ich <strong>ging</strong> · kommen → ich <strong>kam</strong>.</p></div></div><p>불규칙 동사는 과거 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어간<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어간</span>동사원형에서 끝의 -en(-n)을 뗀 부분이에요. 여기에 인칭어미를 붙여요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen → lern-</span></span></span>을 외워야 해요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어미<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어미</span>단어 끝에 붙어 문법 정보를 나타내는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lern-e · gut-er · Kind-er</span></span></span>는 ich·er에 붙지 않아요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-first\"><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>어미</th><th>gehen</th><th>kommen</th><th>sehen</th><th>fahren</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ich</td><td>—</td><td>ging</td><td>kam</td><td>sah</td><td>fuhr</td></tr><tr><td>du</td><td>-st</td><td>ging<span class=\"x-e\">st</span></td><td>kam<span class=\"x-e\">st</span></td><td>sah<span class=\"x-e\">st</span></td><td>fuhr<span class=\"x-e\">st</span></td></tr><tr><td>er · sie · es</td><td>—</td><td>ging</td><td>kam</td><td>sah</td><td>fuhr</td></tr><tr><td>wir</td><td>-en</td><td>ging<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>kam<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>sah<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>fuhr<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td>-t</td><td>ging<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>kam<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>sah<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>fuhr<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td></tr><tr><td>sie · Sie</td><td>-en</td><td>ging<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>kam<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>sah<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>fuhr<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>모음이 바뀌는 패턴</h3><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>패턴</th><th>동사 → 과거 어간</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ei → ie / i</td><td>schreiben → schr<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>b · bleiben → bl<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>b · reiten → r<span class=\"x-e\">i</span>tt</td></tr><tr><td>i → a</td><td>trinken → tr<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nk · finden → f<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nd · singen → s<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>ng · beginnen → beg<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nn</td></tr><tr><td>e → a</td><td>sprechen → spr<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>ch · helfen → h<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>lf · nehmen → n<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>hm · geben → g<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>b · sehen → s<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>h · lesen → l<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>s · essen → <span class=\"x-e\">aß</span></td></tr><tr><td>a → u</td><td>fahren → f<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>hr · tragen → tr<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>g · waschen → w<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>sch</td></tr><tr><td>a → ie</td><td>schlafen → schl<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>f · fallen → f<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>l · laufen → l<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>f · halten → h<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>lt</td></tr><tr><td>그 밖</td><td>gehen → ging · kommen → kam · stehen → stand · sitzen → saß · tun → tat · ziehen → zog</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">분리동사의 과거형</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">분리동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">분리동사</span>앞부분(접두어)이 문장 끝으로 떨어져 나가는 동사예요. 접두어에 강세가 있어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: aufstehen → Ich stehe um 7 Uhr auf.</span></span></span>는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>에서도 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">접두어<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">접두어</span>단어 앞에 붙어 뜻을 더하거나 바꾸는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: auf-stehen · ver-stehen</span></span></span>가 문장 끝으로 가요 — Ich <strong>stand</strong> um sieben Uhr <strong>auf</strong>. · Der Zug <strong>kam</strong> pünktlich <strong>an</strong>.</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">불규칙 동사 과거형</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Gestern ____ ich ins Kino. <span class=\"qh\">gehen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) gehte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) ging</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) gingte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) gang</button></div><div class=\"qe\">불규칙 → ging, ich는 어미 없음.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Er ____ einen Brief. <span class=\"qh\">schreiben</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) schrieb</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) schrob</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) schreibte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) schrieben</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ei → ie.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Wir ____ Kaffee. <span class=\"qh\">trinken</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) trinkten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) trankten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) tranken</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) trank</button></div><div class=\"qe\">i → a, wir → -en.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> ____ du den Film? <span class=\"qh\">sehen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Sahest</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Sahst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Siehst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Sah</button></div><div class=\"qe\">sehen → sah, du → -st.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Der Zug ____ pünktlich ____. <span class=\"qh\">ankommen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) kommte … an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) ankam … —</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) kamt … an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) kam … an</button></div><div class=\"qe\">과거 어간 kam, 접두어 an은 끝.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Sie ____ lange. <span class=\"qh\">그녀는 오래 잤어요 (schlafen)</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) schlief</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) schlief es</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) schlafte sie</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) schlafte</button></div><div class=\"qe\">a → ie.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-E\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">E</span><h2>혼합 동사 — 모음이 바뀌고 -te</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">몇몇 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 모음도 바뀌고 -te도 붙어요 — denken → ich <strong>dachte</strong> · bringen → ich <strong>brachte</strong>.</p></div></div><p>불규칙처럼 모음이 바뀌지만 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어미<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어미</span>단어 끝에 붙어 문법 정보를 나타내는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lern-e · gut-er · Kind-er</span></span></span>는 규칙 동사처럼 -te예요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거분사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거분사</span>완료형과 수동태를 만들 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 대부분 ge-로 시작해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: gelernt · gegangen · verstanden</span></span></span>도 같은 모양이에요(12과).</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>원형</th><th>과거형</th><th>과거분사</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>denken 생각하다</td><td>d<span class=\"x-e\">ach</span>te</td><td>ged<span class=\"x-e\">ach</span>t</td></tr><tr><td>bringen 가져오다</td><td>br<span class=\"x-e\">ach</span>te</td><td>gebr<span class=\"x-e\">ach</span>t</td></tr><tr><td>kennen 알다</td><td>k<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nnte</td><td>gek<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nnt</td></tr><tr><td>wissen 알다</td><td>w<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>sste</td><td>gew<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>sst</td></tr><tr><td>nennen 부르다</td><td>n<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nnte</td><td>gen<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nnt</td></tr><tr><td>rennen 달리다</td><td>r<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nnte</td><td>ger<span class=\"x-e\">a</span>nnt</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-F\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">F</span><h2>sein · haben · werden · 화법조동사</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">말할 때도 가장 자주 쓰는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>이에요 — war · hatte · wurde · konnte · musste.</p></div></div><p>말할 때도 과거형으로 쓰는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>들이에요. 통째로 외워요.</p><h3>sein · haben · werden</h3><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-first\"><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>sein</th><th>haben</th><th>werden</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ich</td><td><strong>war</strong></td><td><strong>hatte</strong></td><td><strong>wurde</strong></td></tr><tr><td>du</td><td>warst</td><td>hattest</td><td>wurdest</td></tr><tr><td>er · sie · es</td><td><strong>war</strong></td><td><strong>hatte</strong></td><td><strong>wurde</strong></td></tr><tr><td>wir</td><td>waren</td><td>hatten</td><td>wurden</td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td>wart</td><td>hattet</td><td>wurdet</td></tr><tr><td>sie · Sie</td><td>waren</td><td>hatten</td><td>wurden</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>화법조동사</h3><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-first t-wide\"><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>können</th><th>müssen</th><th>dürfen</th><th>wollen</th><th>sollen</th><th>mögen</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ich</td><td><strong>konnte</strong></td><td><strong>musste</strong></td><td><strong>durfte</strong></td><td><strong>wollte</strong></td><td><strong>sollte</strong></td><td><strong>mochte</strong></td></tr><tr><td>du</td><td>konntest</td><td>musstest</td><td>durftest</td><td>wolltest</td><td>solltest</td><td>mochtest</td></tr><tr><td>er · sie · es</td><td><strong>konnte</strong></td><td><strong>musste</strong></td><td><strong>durfte</strong></td><td><strong>wollte</strong></td><td><strong>sollte</strong></td><td><strong>mochte</strong></td></tr><tr><td>wir</td><td>konnten</td><td>mussten</td><td>durften</td><td>wollten</td><td>sollten</td><td>mochten</td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td>konntet</td><td>musstet</td><td>durftet</td><td>wolltet</td><td>solltet</td><td>mochtet</td></tr><tr><td>sie · Sie</td><td>konnten</td><td>mussten</td><td>durften</td><td>wollten</td><td>sollten</td><td>mochten</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-key\"><span class=\"co-badge \">화법조동사 과거형에는 움라우트가 없어요</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">können → k<span class=\"x-e\">o</span>nnte · müssen → m<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>sste · dürfen → d<span class=\"x-e\">u</span>rfte · mögen → m<span class=\"x-e\">o</span>chte.<br><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">움라우트<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">움라우트</span>a·o·u 위에 점 두 개를 찍은 ä·ö·ü예요. 복수형·비교급·동사변화에서 모음이 이렇게 바뀌는 일이 많아요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Apfel → die Äpfel · alt → älter</span></span></span>가 붙은 könnte·müsste·dürfte는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">접속법<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">접속법</span>사실이 아닌 일, 바람, 정중함, 남의 말을 나타내는 동사 형태예요(Konjunktiv).<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich hätte gern … · Er sagt, er sei krank.</span></span></span> II(30과)라서 '~⁠할 수 있을 텐데'라는 다른 뜻이에요.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">möchten의 과거</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">möchten은 과거형이 따로 없어서 wollte로 말해요 — Ich <strong>wollte</strong> ins Kino gehen. 영화 보러 가고 싶었어요.</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">sein · haben · 화법조동사 과거형</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Gestern ____ ich krank.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) ware</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) warte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) war</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) wurde</button></div><div class=\"qe\">sein → war.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Wir ____ keine Zeit.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) habten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) hätten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) hatte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) hatten</button></div><div class=\"qe\">haben → hatten.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Ich ____ gestern nicht kommen. <span class=\"qh\">갈 수 없었어요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) konntet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) kann</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) konnte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) könnte</button></div><div class=\"qe\">과거 → konnte, 움라우트 없음.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Er ____ früh aufstehen. <span class=\"qh\">일찍 일어나야 했어요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) muss</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) mussten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) müsste</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) musste</button></div><div class=\"qe\">화법조동사는 과거형에서 움라우트가 빠져요 — müssen → musste.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Es ____ dunkel. <span class=\"qh\">어두워졌어요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) wird</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) wurde</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) war</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) würde</button></div><div class=\"qe\">werden → wurde.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Als Kind ____ ich keinen Spinat. <span class=\"qh\">어릴 때 시금치를 싫어했어요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) mochte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) möchte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) mögte</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) mag</button></div><div class=\"qe\">mögen → mochte.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-G\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">G</span><h2>화법조동사의 현재완료</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">화법조동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">화법조동사</span>능력·허락·의무·의지 같은 뜻을 더해 주는 동사예요. 본동사는 원형으로 문장 끝에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: können · dürfen · müssen · sollen · wollen · mögen</span></span></span>를 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재완료<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재완료</span>말할 때 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. haben/sein + 과거분사로 만들어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.</span></span></span>로 쓰면 끝에 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">원형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">원형</span>동사원형을 줄여 부르는 말이에요. 사전에 실린 동사의 기본 모양으로, 대부분 -en으로 끝나요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen · gehen · arbeiten</span></span></span>이 두 개 와요 — Ich habe arbeiten <strong>müssen</strong>. 보통은 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span> musste를 더 많이 써요.</p></div></div><p>화법조동사의 현재완료는 끝에 원형이 두 개 와요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">본동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">본동사</span>화법조동사·보조 동사와 함께 쓰일 때, 실제 뜻을 나타내는 동사예요. 문장 끝에 원형이나 과거분사로 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich kann gut schwimmen. → schwimmen</span></span></span> 원형 다음에 화법조동사 원형이에요.</p><div class=\"klam\"><div class=\"klam-cells\"><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">1</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">Ich</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-v\"><span class=\"klam-pos\"><b class=\"kn\">2</b></span><span class=\"klam-w\">habe</span></div><div class=\"klam-c \"><span class=\"klam-w\">gestern</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-inf\"><span class=\"klam-w\">arbeiten</span></div><div class=\"klam-c klam-inf\"><span class=\"klam-w\">müssen</span></div></div><div class=\"klam-tr\">어제 일해야 했어요.</div></div><div class=\"exl\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich <strong>habe</strong> nicht kommen <strong>können</strong>. = Ich <strong>konnte</strong> nicht kommen.</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">갈 수 없었어요.</span></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">과거형이 더 자연스러워요</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">화법조동사는 말할 때도 과거형을 훨씬 많이 써요 — Ich musste gestern arbeiten.<br>원형 두 개짜리 현재완료는 알아보는 정도로 익혀 두면 돼요.</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-H\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">H</span><h2>세 형태 — 한 세트로 외우기</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">불규칙 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">원형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">원형</span>동사원형을 줄여 부르는 말이에요. 사전에 실린 동사의 기본 모양으로, 대부분 -en으로 끝나요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen · gehen · arbeiten</span></span></span>·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거분사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거분사</span>완료형과 수동태를 만들 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 대부분 ge-로 시작해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: gelernt · gegangen · verstanden</span></span></span>를 한 세트로 외워요 — gehen · ging · gegangen.</p></div></div><p>sein과 쓰는 동사에는 ist를 붙였어요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left\"><thead><tr><th>원형</th><th>과거형</th><th>과거분사</th><th>뜻</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>beginnen</td><td>begann</td><td>begonnen</td><td>시작하다</td></tr><tr><td>bleiben</td><td>blieb</td><td>ist geblieben</td><td>머물다</td></tr><tr><td>bringen</td><td>brachte</td><td>gebracht</td><td>가져오다</td></tr><tr><td>denken</td><td>dachte</td><td>gedacht</td><td>생각하다</td></tr><tr><td>essen</td><td>aß</td><td>gegessen</td><td>먹다</td></tr><tr><td>fahren</td><td>fuhr</td><td>ist gefahren</td><td>타고 가다</td></tr><tr><td>fallen</td><td>fiel</td><td>ist gefallen</td><td>떨어지다</td></tr><tr><td>finden</td><td>fand</td><td>gefunden</td><td>찾다</td></tr><tr><td>fliegen</td><td>flog</td><td>ist geflogen</td><td>날다</td></tr><tr><td>geben</td><td>gab</td><td>gegeben</td><td>주다</td></tr><tr><td>gehen</td><td>ging</td><td>ist gegangen</td><td>가다</td></tr><tr><td>halten</td><td>hielt</td><td>gehalten</td><td>붙잡다·멈추다</td></tr><tr><td>helfen</td><td>half</td><td>geholfen</td><td>돕다</td></tr><tr><td>kennen</td><td>kannte</td><td>gekannt</td><td>알다</td></tr><tr><td>kommen</td><td>kam</td><td>ist gekommen</td><td>오다</td></tr><tr><td>laufen</td><td>lief</td><td>ist gelaufen</td><td>달리다</td></tr><tr><td>lesen</td><td>las</td><td>gelesen</td><td>읽다</td></tr><tr><td>liegen</td><td>lag</td><td>gelegen</td><td>놓여 있다</td></tr><tr><td>nehmen</td><td>nahm</td><td>genommen</td><td>잡다</td></tr><tr><td>rufen</td><td>rief</td><td>gerufen</td><td>부르다</td></tr><tr><td>schlafen</td><td>schlief</td><td>geschlafen</td><td>자다</td></tr><tr><td>schreiben</td><td>schrieb</td><td>geschrieben</td><td>쓰다</td></tr><tr><td>schwimmen</td><td>schwamm</td><td>ist geschwommen</td><td>헤엄치다</td></tr><tr><td>sehen</td><td>sah</td><td>gesehen</td><td>보다</td></tr><tr><td>sitzen</td><td>saß</td><td>gesessen</td><td>앉아 있다</td></tr><tr><td>sprechen</td><td>sprach</td><td>gesprochen</td><td>말하다</td></tr><tr><td>stehen</td><td>stand</td><td>gestanden</td><td>서 있다</td></tr><tr><td>sterben</td><td>starb</td><td>ist gestorben</td><td>죽다</td></tr><tr><td>tragen</td><td>trug</td><td>getragen</td><td>나르다·입다</td></tr><tr><td>treffen</td><td>traf</td><td>getroffen</td><td>만나다</td></tr><tr><td>trinken</td><td>trank</td><td>getrunken</td><td>마시다</td></tr><tr><td>tun</td><td>tat</td><td>getan</td><td>하다</td></tr><tr><td>vergessen</td><td>vergaß</td><td>vergessen</td><td>잊다</td></tr><tr><td>verlieren</td><td>verlor</td><td>verloren</td><td>잃다</td></tr><tr><td>werden</td><td>wurde</td><td>ist geworden</td><td>되다</td></tr><tr><td>wissen</td><td>wusste</td><td>gewusst</td><td>알다</td></tr><tr><td>ziehen</td><td>zog</td><td>gezogen / ist gezogen</td><td>끌다 / 이사하다</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>같은 모음 패턴끼리 묶어 외우기</h3><p>알파벳 순서보다 모음이 바뀌는 패턴으로 묶으면 훨씬 쉽게 외워요. 위 표의 동사를 패턴별로 나누면 이렇게 돼요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>모음 패턴</th><th>동사</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ei – ie – ie</td><td>bleiben – blieb – geblieben<br>schreiben – schrieb – geschrieben</td></tr><tr><td>ie – o – o</td><td>fliegen – flog – geflogen<br>verlieren – verlor – verloren<br>ziehen – zog – gezogen</td></tr><tr><td>i – a – u</td><td>finden – fand – gefunden<br>trinken – trank – getrunken</td></tr><tr><td>i – a – o</td><td>beginnen – begann – begonnen<br>schwimmen – schwamm – geschwommen</td></tr><tr><td>e – a – o</td><td>helfen – half – geholfen<br>sprechen – sprach – gesprochen<br>nehmen – nahm – genommen<br>treffen – traf – getroffen<br>sterben – starb – gestorben</td></tr><tr><td>e – a – e</td><td>geben – gab – gegeben<br>lesen – las – gelesen<br>sehen – sah – gesehen<br>essen – aß – gegessen<br>vergessen – vergaß – vergessen</td></tr><tr><td>a – u – a</td><td>fahren – fuhr – gefahren<br>tragen – trug – getragen</td></tr><tr><td>원형 모음 – ie – 원형 모음</td><td>fallen – fiel – gefallen<br>halten – hielt – gehalten<br>schlafen – schlief – geschlafen<br>laufen – lief – gelaufen<br>rufen – rief – gerufen</td></tr><tr><td>혼합 동사 (-te · -t)</td><td>bringen – brachte – gebracht<br>denken – dachte – gedacht<br>kennen – kannte – gekannt<br>wissen – wusste – gewusst</td></tr><tr><td>따로 외우기</td><td>gehen – ging – gegangen<br>kommen – kam – gekommen<br>stehen – stand – gestanden<br>sitzen – saß – gesessen<br>liegen – lag – gelegen<br>tun – tat – getan<br>werden – wurde – geworden</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"dgm-note\">원형 모음 – ie – 원형 모음은 과거형에만 ie가 오고, 과거분사는 원형의 모음 그대로예요 — schlafen – schlief – geschlafen.</div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-I\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">I</span><h2>가장 많이 하는 실수</h2></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 1</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">불규칙 동사에 -te를 붙여요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich gehte nach Hause.<span class=\"tx-n\">규칙 동사처럼</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich ging nach Hause.<span class=\"tx-n\">집에 갔어요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">불규칙 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 과거 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어간<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어간</span>동사원형에서 끝의 -en(-n)을 뗀 부분이에요. 여기에 인칭어미를 붙여요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen → lern-</span></span></span>을 따로 외워요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 2</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">화법조동사 과거형에 움라우트를 붙여요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich könnte gestern nicht kommen.<span class=\"tx-n\">접속법 II</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich konnte gestern nicht kommen.<span class=\"tx-n\">어제 못 갔어요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>은 konnte·musste·durfte·mochte, <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">움라우트<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">움라우트</span>a·o·u 위에 점 두 개를 찍은 ä·ö·ü예요. 복수형·비교급·동사변화에서 모음이 이렇게 바뀌는 일이 많아요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Apfel → die Äpfel · alt → älter</span></span></span>가 없어요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 3</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">혼합 동사를 규칙 동사로 써요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich denkte an dich.<span class=\"tx-n\">denk + te</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich dachte an dich.<span class=\"tx-n\">네 생각을 했어</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">denken·bringen·kennen·wissen은 모음이 바뀌어요 — dachte · brachte · kannte · wusste.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 4</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">불규칙 동사 du에 -st를 빼요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Du kam spät.<span class=\"tx-n\">ich·er 모양</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Du kamst spät.<span class=\"tx-n\">너 늦게 왔어</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어미<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어미</span>단어 끝에 붙어 문법 정보를 나타내는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lern-e · gut-er · Kind-er</span></span></span>가 없는 건 ich와 er뿐이에요.</div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">실수 피하기</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Wir fuhren nach Italien.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Wir fuhrten nach Italien.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Wir führen nach Italien.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Wir fahrten nach Italien.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">fahren → fuhr, wir → fuhren.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Ich weißte die Antwort nicht.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ich wusst die Antwort nicht.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Ich wisste die Antwort nicht.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Ich wusste die Antwort nicht.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">wissen → wusste.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Sie durft nicht ausgehen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Sie darfte nicht ausgehen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Sie durfte nicht ausgehen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Sie dürfte nicht ausgehen.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">dürfen의 과거형은 움라우트가 빠진 durfte예요 — müssen → musste와 같아요.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Er brachtet mir Blumen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Er brachte mir Blumen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Er brang mir Blumen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Er bringte mir Blumen.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">bringen → brachte.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Ihr war sehr nett.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ihr waret sehr nett.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Ihr wartet sehr nett.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Ihr wart sehr nett.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">sein → ihr wart.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-J\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">J</span><h2>참고</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">과거형과 접속법 II</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">hatte·war·konnte(과거)와 hätte·wäre·könnte(<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">접속법<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">접속법</span>사실이 아닌 일, 바람, 정중함, 남의 말을 나타내는 동사 형태예요(Konjunktiv).<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich hätte gern … · Er sagt, er sei krank.</span></span></span> II)는 모양이 비슷해요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">움라우트<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">움라우트</span>a·o·u 위에 점 두 개를 찍은 ä·ö·ü예요. 복수형·비교급·동사변화에서 모음이 이렇게 바뀌는 일이 많아요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Apfel → die Äpfel · alt → älter</span></span></span> 하나로 뜻이 달라지니 30과에서 함께 정리해요.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">이야기의 시간 접속사 als</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">과거의 한 시점은 als로 말해요 — <strong>Als</strong> ich ein Kind war, wohnten wir in Busan. 어렸을 때 우리는 부산에 살았어요(27과).</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">지역 차이</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">독일 북부에서는 말할 때도 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>을 비교적 자주 쓰고, 남부에서는 sein까지 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재완료<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재완료</span>말할 때 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. haben/sein + 과거분사로 만들어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe Deutsch gelernt.</span></span></span>로 말하기도 해요 — Ich bin krank gewesen.<br>시험에서는 이 과의 기준을 따르면 돼요.</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-K\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">K</span><h2>바로 쓰는 문장 · 일상 회화</h2></div><p>말할 때도 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">과거형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">과거형</span>글과 이야기에서 주로 쓰는 과거 시제예요. 동사 하나로 과거를 나타내요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lernte · ich ging · ich war</span></span></span>으로 쓰는 문장이에요.</p><div class=\"exl talk-l\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Gestern <strong>war</strong> ich krank.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">게스턴 바 이히 크랑크</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">어제 아팠어요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich <strong>hatte</strong> keine Zeit.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">이히 하테 카이네 차이트</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">시간이 없었어요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich <strong>konnte</strong> nicht kommen.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">이히 콘테 니히트 콤멘</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">갈 수가 없었어요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Es <strong>gab</strong> ein Problem.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">에스 갑 아인 프로블렘</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">문제가 하나 있었어요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Das <strong>wusste</strong> ich nicht.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">다스 부스테 이히 니히트</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">그건 몰랐어요.</span></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"summary\"><div class=\"summary-card\"><h2 class=\"sum-title\">이 과 정리</h2><div><div class=\"sum-li\">말할 때는 현재완료, 글·이야기·뉴스는 과거형 — sein·haben·화법조동사는 말할 때도 과거형</div><div class=\"sum-li\">규칙 동사는 어간 + te + 어미, 어간 -t·-d는 -ete — lernte · arbeitete</div><div class=\"sum-li\">불규칙 동사는 과거 어간을 외우고, ich·er는 어미 없음 — ging · kam · sah · fuhr</div><div class=\"sum-li\">혼합 동사 — dachte · brachte · kannte · wusste</div><div class=\"sum-li\">war · hatte · wurde, 화법조동사는 konnte · musste · durfte · wollte · sollte · mochte (움라우트 없음)</div><div class=\"sum-li\">화법조동사의 현재완료는 원형 두 개 — Ich habe arbeiten müssen.</div><div class=\"sum-li\">불규칙 동사는 원형 · 과거형 · 과거분사를 한 줄로 외워요</div></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\" style=\"margin-top:20px\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">다음 ⏭ 14과</span><div>14과부터 전치사를 배워요. 먼저 늘 4격과 쓰는 전치사(für·ohne·durch…)와 늘 3격과 쓰는 전치사(mit·bei·nach·zu…)를 정리해요.<br>전치사 뒤의 관사도 3과의 변화표를 그대로 써요.</div></div></section><section id=\"solutions\" class=\"solutions\"><h2 class=\"sol-title\">Lösungen — 정답 모아보기</h2><div class=\"sol-grid\"><div><b>10–12과 복습</b>1. bin · 2. besucht · 3. hat · 4. Ich muss um 7 Uhr aufstehen.</div><div><b>규칙 동사 과거형</b>1. arbeitete · 2. wohnten · 3. studierte · 4. Spieltest</div><div><b>불규칙 동사 과거형</b>1. ging · 2. schrieb · 3. tranken · 4. Sahst · 5. kam … an · 6. schlief</div><div><b>sein · haben · 화법조동사 과거형</b>1. war · 2. hatten · 3. konnte · 4. musste · 5. wurde · 6. mochte</div><div><b>실수 피하기</b>1. Wir fuhren nach Italien. · 2. Ich wusste die Antwort nicht. · 3. Sie durfte nicht ausgehen. · 4. Er brachte mir Blumen. · 5. Ihr wart sehr nett.</div></div></section>\n<div class=\"brand-foot\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"foot-logo\"><div class=\"foot-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div><div class=\"foot-tag\">Innovative Learning Beyond the Traditional</div></div>\n"